<section class="wrap section" aria-label="How import works">
  <div class="steps g1-sm">
    <article class="card">
      <span class="hint">1. Bring the JSON</span>
      <h2>Paste, upload, or send it from a script</h2>
      <p>
        The Import from Grafana button in the chat, <span class="mono">observe import</span>, or
        the <span class="mono">import_grafana_dashboard</span> MCP tool. Classic model, external
        share exports and API responses all work.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="hint">2. Match datasources</span>
      <h2>Your Grafana uids map to your datasources</h2>
      <p>
        Matches come from <span class="mono">grafanaUids</span> in the datasources file.
        SlashObserve never guesses between two of the same type: it asks.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="hint">3. Read the report</span>
      <h2>Every query runs once, and you see the result</h2>
      <p>
        Panels that fail are saved as unverified, not dropped. Unsupported panels become
        placeholders that say why.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

